From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 26 Feb 2026 03:28:20 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: report configured-but-not-started STA in phy_status

In AP+STA mode, hostapd's startup state machine queries phy_status
before wpa_supplicant has started the STA interface (deferred via
config_set defer=1). The NOT_FOUND response causes hostapd to
conclude no STA exists and skip setting start_disabled on the AP,
which then enters DFS/ACS and conflicts with the STA starting
shortly after, creating a teardown/retry loop.

Return a NOT_STARTED state when interfaces are configured in phy.data
but not yet present in wpas.interfaces, so hostapd correctly sets
start_disabled=1 and waits for the STA to connect.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 openwrt/files/wpa_supplicant.uc |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/openwrt/files/wpa_supplicant.uc
+++ b/openwrt/files/wpa_supplicant.uc
@@ -632,6 +632,9 @@ let main_obj = {
 				}
 			}
 
+			if (length(ifnames) > 0)
+				return { state: "NOT_STARTED" };
+
 			return libubus.STATUS_NOT_FOUND;
 		}
 	},
